CHANGELOG
=========

0.16.3: 2026-11-23
-------------------

Environment-variable expansion in file paths (finding 194):

- I/O & paths: added URL-safe ``expand_env_vars`` and ``expand_location`` in
  ``vith/io/backends.py`` (re-exported in ``vith.io``) wrapping
  ``os.path.expandvars`` and ``os.path.expanduser``, fixing Windows
  PowerShell/CLI paths like ``vith %APPDATA%\alacritty\alacritty.toml`` as well
  as ``$VAR`` / ``${VAR}`` across platforms while leaving ``scheme://...`` URLs
  untouched (194).
- Buffers, Ex commands & completion: expanded env vars during buffer creation,
  buffer deduplication, writes/overwrite guards, ``:e`` / ``:w`` / ``:w >>`` /
  ``:r`` / ``:cd`` / ``:so`` / ``:sp`` / ``:vsp`` / ``:tabe`` / ``:sav`` /
  ``:f``, ``-u`` / config / hook discovery, and command-line path completion
  (``_EnvPathCompleter``). On Windows, ``_match_windows_env_var`` in
  ``vith/commands/handler.py`` recognizes defined ``%VAR%`` tokens in Ex
  commands without breaking Vim's ``%`` / ``%:p`` filename tokens or ``:!``
  shell commands.
- Tests: added URL-preservation, CLI/Ex/completion/config env-var expansion
  tests in ``tests/test_io_backends.py``.

0.16.2: 2026-11-23
-------------------

Windows ConPTY Thai/Lao input fix (finding 193):

- Windows input: patch ``prompt_toolkit.input.win32``'s
  ``Vt100ConsoleInputReader._get_keys`` and ``ConsoleInputReader._get_keys``
  (with signature verification and rollback support) to accept synthesized
  Alt+Numpad ``VK_MENU`` (``0x12``) key-up Unicode deliveries emitted by
  Windows ConPTY (``conhost.exe``) for non-``C3_ALPHA`` characters — fixing
  dropped Thai/Lao upper/lower vowels, tone marks, ``ฯ``, ``ๆ``, ``฿``, and
  Thai/Lao digits during both typing and bracketed paste (193).
- Tests: added Win32 ConPTY ``VK_MENU`` key-up and rollback regression tests
  in ``tests/test_thai.py``.

0.16.1: 2026-11-23
-------------------

Correctness fixes from the Round 11 deep audit and a user field report (findings 167–192):

- Critical/high: bare ``:!{cmd}`` now schedules prompt-toolkit's async
  ``run_system_command`` instead of dropping the coroutine (167); ``*`` / ``#``
  normalize ``KeyPressEvent.arg`` so they no longer crash (168); CSV/TSV cells
  are rendered as literal text instead of Rich markup (169) and bare carriage
  returns no longer raise ``csv.Error`` (182); ``:j`` / ``:join`` report ``E488``
  for non-numeric counts (170).
- Live ``:render``: generic renderer errors now show a diagnostic rather than
  being silently labeled ``stale`` (171), ``_has_good_render`` is reset on
  diagnostics (172), multi-line error messages stay line-aligned (173),
  ``immediate=True`` survives render coalescing (183), and custom
  ``[render.commands]`` keys resolve across filetype aliases (184).
- Ex commands / options: ``:set ff?`` queries work and ``:setlocal all`` lists
  options (174, 186); bare ``:s`` reuses a dedicated last-substitute pattern
  instead of the shared search state (175); ``:sort n`` is stable and its ``!``
  form reverses ties like Vim (176); ``:d`` / ``:y`` with a named register also
  update the unnamed register (187).
- Editor / config: ``:e`` reload clears stale undo history (177) and guards
  untitled buffers (189); ``cold_text_compression`` config is type-validated
  and ``cold_text_compression_level`` accepts zstd levels up to 22 (178, 188);
  configured ``fileformat`` is honored by new buffers (179); ``create_tab`` on
  an empty arrangement no longer creates two tabs (180).
- Thai / robustness: visual-block highlight agrees with yank on short rows
  (181); reporter diagnostics recover from executor exceptions (190);
  unassigned ``U+0EC7`` is no longer treated as a combining mark (191).
- Tab in Insert mode now inserts an indentation step anywhere on the line
  instead of falling through to completion (192), and the default is Vim's
  ``noexpandtab`` (``expand_tab = False``), so a plain Tab inserts a literal
  tab character; ``:set expandtab`` still switches to spaces.
- Documentation: ``docs/live_render.md`` config table corrected (185); bug
  bundle synced to 192 findings (191 fixed, 1 withdrawn).

Verification: **558 passed**, 89.24% coverage, mypy clean (88 files), ruff clean.

0.16.0: 2026-11-22
-------------------

Live async ``:render`` split preview & Round 10 deep performance / algorithmic optimizations:

Live async ``:render`` split preview (``docs/live_render.md``):

- Added real-time asynchronous preview split Ex commands ``:render[!]``,
  ``:render-split-v[!]`` (editor left, preview right), and ``:render-split-h[!]``
  (editor top, preview bottom) in ``vith/render.py`` and
  ``vith/commands/render.py``, keeping keyboard focus in the editing pane via
  backward-compatible ``after=True`` / ``focus_new=False`` split placement in
  ``WindowArrangement``.
- Added optional ``vith[render]`` packaging extra (``rich>=13.0.0``,
  ``rich-rst>=1.3.0``) with zero eager imports on cold startup; supports
  Markdown (headings, bold/italic/underline, tables, Pygments fenced code blocks,
  Thai/Lao text), reStructuredText (``allow_file_access=False``), JSON (retaining
  the last valid preview with a ``stale`` title while mid-edit), CSV/TSV tables
  (capped at 5,000 rows), built-in ANSI escape logs, Rich Syntax fallback, and
  custom external CLI renderers via ``[render.commands]``.
- Converted Rich ``Console.render_lines()`` ``Segment`` output directly into
  cached ``prompt_toolkit`` ``StyleAndTextTuples`` (with ``console.options.update_width``
  width locking and fragment coalescing) and wired an ``O(1)``
  ``DocumentLexer`` fast path with ``_rendered_version`` invalidation,
  preview chrome suppression in ``vith/layout.py``, and sticky Thai/Lao
  ``SARA AM`` gate latching.
- Implemented single-flight debounced background rendering (``render_debounce_ms``
  with max-wait ceiling and edit coalescing), automatic terminal/split resize
  re-rendering, heading/landmark-anchored cursor & viewport scroll sync
  (auto-paused when focused in the preview pane), and lazy ``Document._cache``
  preservation (``_source_row_and_line_count`` + precomputed
  ``_preview_line_starts``) for near-zero editing overhead.
- Added validated ``[render]`` (``default_split``, ``debounce_ms``,
  ``sync_scroll``) and ``[render.commands]`` TOML configuration in
  ``vith/rc_file.py`` and ``examples/config/config.toml``, plus full OKF v0.2
  technical documentation in ``docs/live_render.md``.

Round 10 deep performance & algorithmic audit (findings 155–166; 159 archived):

- Startup & rendering (155, 156, 163): resolved ``FiletypeTabstops`` through
  Pygments ``_mapping`` without eagerly importing 32 lexer modules; added
  tab-free fast path & cached ``_try_char`` in ``TabsProcessor``; cached
  ``SARA AM`` screen rows, filtered ``copy_body`` margin first, and optimized
  Visual Block selection in ``vith/thai/patches.py``.
- Keystroke latency & completion caching (157, 164): eliminated ``O(file size)``
  ``Document.current_line`` copies with ``O(line length)`` ``current_line_and_col``
  and ASCII-fast ``_on_text_changed``; tracked ``ColdTextBuffer._non_cursor_version``
  in ``DocumentWordsCompleter`` to invalidate non-cursor edits while keeping P3
  typing cache hits.
- Ex commands & lexer memory (158, 160, 161, 162): replaced ``O(N^2)`` string
  concatenation in ``:join``; compiled non-case ``:substitute`` replacements to
  C ``re.sub`` templates with ``O(A log A)`` overlap checking; cached ``:norm``
  ``KeyProcessor`` with batched ``_on_text_changed`` and row-anchor tracking;
  capped ``DocumentLexer`` ``line_generators``, guarded out-of-range EOF drains,
  and replaced 215-module ``guess_lexer`` with deterministic
  ``sniff_filetype_from_text``.
- Thai/Lao algorithms & secondary hot spots (165, 166): single-pass
  ``_compute_cell_columns``, UTF-32 ``libthai`` buffer, ``O(log W)`` ``bisect``
  word motions, ``>>`` splice, ``:w >>`` append, ``_read`` CR guard,
  ``:sort nu``, ``DirectoryIO`` ``scandir``, static ``:g/pat/m N``, and
  single-pass ``FiletypeCompleter`` (finding 159 withdrawn when the earlier
  experimental ``:render`` prototype was reverted).
- Full test suite passing: 531 passed (88.98% coverage), mypy clean on 87
  source files (Python 3.10 target), ruff clean.

0.15.1: 2026-11-20
-------------------

Tab-aware Thai/CJK/ASCII cursor motion & visual blocks, plus Round 9 hardening:

Tab-aware visual-column motion & visual-block editing (finding 154):

- Expanded ``\t`` to the buffer's effective ``tabstop`` (global, per-filetype,
  buffer-local ``:set`` / ``:setlocal ts=N``, and per-split safe) in
  ``vith/thai/clusters.py`` visual-column helpers (guarding ASCII fast paths
  with ``"\t" not in line``) and ``ColdTextBuffer._cursor_vertical`` (with
  mid-run ``tabstop`` re-anchoring), so ``j``/``k`` stay locked on the same
  visual column across Thai combining marks, CJK, empty lines, and tabs.
- Rewrote ``SelectionType.BLOCK`` in ``_thai_selection_ranges`` and
  ``_thai_selection_range_at_line`` directly in display columns across
  ``from_line..to_line`` so shorter tabbed lines are no longer dropped by
  codepoint-length checks, and fixed upstream ``prompt_toolkit``'s
  ``TextObject.operator_range`` ``BLOCK`` upper-corner off-by-one so
  ``<C-v>`` highlight, ``y``, ``d``, ``I``, and ``A`` align with Vim in all
  four drag directions.
- Patched ``Document.get_column_cursor_position`` (``{count}|``) and
  ``Document.paste_clipboard_data`` so column jumps and visual-block ``p``/``P``
  align on display columns (and charwise ``p`` lands after the full Thai cell
  cluster instead of splitting combining marks).

Round 9 audit improvements (findings 151–153, all closed):

- Performance (151): added ``splice_buffer_lines`` / ``splice_lines_at`` /
  ``apply_deleted_range`` for contiguous Ex edits; retained inactive live tab
  frames/scroll/lexers across tab switches; replaced quadratic ``:g`` move/copy
  loops with ``O(n)`` static ``0``/``$`` fast paths and ``_IndexedLineChunks``
  (``O(m sqrt(n))``); merged SARA-AM single-pass row scan with visible-buffer
  Thai gate decay/re-latch; cached compiled ``:b`` search regex; hoisted
  ``get_cwidth`` and added tab-free/ASCII fast paths in ``:retab``.
- Deduplication & correctness (152): derived ``Editor._default_options`` and
  ``rc_file._CONFIG_OPTION_MAP`` from the ``:set`` catalog; unified
  ``_resolve_editor_buffer``, ``apply_int_option_value``, 1-based line-address
  resolution, ``resolve_ignore_case``, and write-target normalization (fixing
  the ``:set ro`` symlink bypass and stale dirty flag).
- Readability & public surface (153): consolidated ``vith/lexer.py`` top-level
  imports, ordered ``vith/commands/completer.py`` classes consistently,
  migrated ``vith/cold_text.py`` to direct submodule imports, and moved
  internal compatibility shims in ``vith/thai/__init__.py`` behind PEP 562
  ``__getattr__`` / ``__dir__``.
- Full test suite passing: 505 passed (90.25% coverage), mypy clean on 83
  source files (Python 3.10 target), ruff clean.

0.15.0: 2026-11-20
-------------------

Ex command completeness, Round 8 audit hardening & ``vith/commands/`` modularization:

Ex commands & ``:set`` ergonomics (Phases 1–4):

- Added full Vim Ex command parity across files and configuration:
  ``:[addr]r`` / ``:read`` (files via I/O backends and ``!cmd`` with combined
  ``2>&1`` output), ``:sav`` / ``:saveas`` with strict Vim ``:w {file}`` copy
  semantics, ``:up`` / ``:update``, ``:x`` / ``:xit`` / ``:exit``,
  ``:wa`` / ``:wall``, ``:xa`` / ``:xall``, ``:wqall``, ``:enew`` / ``:ene``,
  ``:f`` / ``:file`` (status & rename), ``:so`` / ``:source`` (in-TUI config
  reload), and ``%`` / ``#`` command-line filename expansion with chainable
  ``:p`` / ``:h`` / ``:t`` / ``:r`` / ``:e`` modifiers.
- Completed buffer, window, and tab Ex commands: ``:ls`` / ``:files``,
  ``:b #`` alternate buffer tracking, ``:bf`` / ``:bfirst``, ``:bl`` / ``:blast``,
  ``:bnext`` / ``:bprev`` / ``:bprevious``, targeted ``:bd`` / ``:bdelete`` /
  ``:bw`` / ``:bwipeout``, ``:sb`` / ``:sbuffer``, ``:clo`` / ``:close``,
  ``:on``, ``:tabo`` / ``:tabonly``, ``:tabfir`` / ``:tabfirst`` /
  ``:tabr`` / ``:tabrewind``, ``:tabl`` / ``:tablast``, ``:tabm`` / ``:tabmove``,
  and ``:tabs``.
- Extracted the shared Ex range engine (``vith/commands/ranges.py``) and added
  generalized bare address jumps (``:$``, ``.``, ``±N``, ``'<``, ``'>``) and
  range line-editing commands: ``:d`` / ``:delete``, ``:y`` / ``:yank``,
  ``:pu`` / ``:put``, ``:m`` / ``:move``, ``:t`` / ``:co`` / ``:copy``,
  ``:j`` / ``:join``, ``:sort``, ``:retab``, ``:g`` / ``:global`` and
  ``:v`` / ``:vglobal``, ``:[range]!{cmd}`` external filter, ``:[range]w``
  (partial write, ``>>`` append, ``!cmd`` pipe), ``:[range]norm[!]`` /
  ``:normal[!]`` isolated key replay, ``:u`` / ``:undo``, ``:red`` / ``:redo``,
  and ``:noh`` / ``:nohlsearch``.
- Upgraded ``:set`` / ``:setlocal`` with bare ``:set``, ``:set all``, queries
  (``opt?``), toggles (``opt!`` / ``invopt``), multi-argument option lists, and
  live preview; added ``smartcase`` (``scs``), ``shiftwidth`` (``sw``),
  ``readonly`` (``ro``), ``autoindent`` (``ai``), ``fileencoding`` (``fenc``),
  and ``fileformat`` (``ff``); rendered all multi-line informational commands
  (``:ls``, ``:ver``, ``:mes``, ``:reg``, ``:marks``, ``:tabs``, ``:set``,
  ``:comp``, ``:help``) in read-only scratch splits via ``Editor.show_info``.

Round 8 audit & hardening (findings 130–150, all closed):

- Exempted the active buffer's own file from the explicit-write overwrite guard
  (``:w %``, ``:wq %``, ``:up %``, ``:x %``, ``:sav <current>``; finding 130);
  shared ``close_or_exit()`` across the quit family and aligned ``ZZ`` with
  ``:x`` so multi-window dirty buffers survive ``:wq`` (131); scoped ``:only``
  to the active tab and added dirty-buffer guards + ``!`` to ``:only``,
  ``:tabclose``, and ``:tabonly`` (132).
- Fixed ``:e`` / ``:e!`` reload crashes on read-only and directory buffers
  (133); synchronized mouse click focus into ``WindowArrangement`` (134);
  published substitute search/replacement state from ``:g/.../s`` (135);
  excluded the ``/`` search toolbar from Insert-mode Tab indentation (136);
  made ``:r !``, ``:[range]!``, and ``:w !`` byte-preserving via UTF-8
  ``surrogateescape`` (137).
- Validated TOML option types/bounds and widened top-level ``.vithrc`` TOML
  detection (138); implemented Vim's ``:s`` replacement dialect (``&``, ``\&``,
  ``~``, ``\r``, ``\n``, ``\0``–``\9``, ``\u``/``\U``/``\l``/``\L``/``\e``/``\E``;
  139); preserved ``fileformat`` (``dos``/``unix``/``mac``) across reads,
  writes, partial writes, and ``:w >>`` (140).
- Measured cell columns with ``get_cwidth`` so double-width CJK/emoji align in
  ``j``/``k`` and visual-block rectangles (141); hardened the shared ReDoS
  guard for overlapping alternations and counted repeats (142); fixed
  ``:[range]normal`` final-address clamping (143), ``:retab`` without ``!`` on
  space-only indents (144), ``:cq`` CLI non-zero exit code propagation (145),
  and ``show_message`` Thai renderer gate latching (146).
- Resolved low-severity Vim deviations (colorscheme ``E185``, ``:f`` path
  normalization, backend ``:w >>``, single-character registers on ``:d``/``:y``/``:pu``,
  ``:setlocal`` validation, smartcase escape handling; 147), dead-code and
  backend-lookup duplication (``find_backend``; 148), algorithm/cache hot spots
  (indexed ``:g`` move/copy, truncated register previews, versioned
  word-completer cache, extensionless lexer sniff retry, ``:reg`` display for
  ``:d``/``:y`` registers; 149), and readability/test/docs cleanups (150).

Architecture & code quality:

- Split the 3,554-line ``vith/commands/commands.py`` monolith into 11 cohesive
  submodules directly under ``vith/commands/`` (``registry``, ``common``,
  ``buffers``, ``tabs``, ``files``, ``options``, ``info``, ``substitution``,
  ``editing``, ``normal``, ``global_cmd``) re-exported via
  ``vith/commands/__init__.py``, and deduplicated shared substitution, range,
  register, file-write, ``:set``/preview, and ``:normal`` helpers.
- Updated ``README.md``, ``vith/help.py``, and the ``docs/`` OKF v0.2 bundle.
- Full test suite passing: 466 passed (89.79% coverage), mypy clean on 79
  source files (Python 3.10 target), ruff clean.

0.14.0: 2026-11-13
-------------------

Tab stops, TOML configuration & ``:s`` substitute enhancements:

Tab stops & rendering:

- Wrapped ``TabsProcessor.apply_transformation`` to calculate tab expansion from
  visual display columns (``get_cwidth``) instead of codepoint counts, fixing
  column alignment with Thai combining marks and double-width CJK characters
  (finding 127).
- Changed the default ``tabstop`` from ``4`` to ``8`` to match Vi/Vim standards
  (finding 127).
- Added per-filetype tab stop defaults (``DEFAULT_FILETYPE_TABSTOPS`` /
  ``FiletypeTabstops``) with canonical alias normalization and 3-tier buffer
  resolution, plus ``:setlocal`` / ``:setl`` support for ``tabstop`` and
  ``filetype`` with live preview and completion (finding 128).

Configuration & hooks:

- Added declarative TOML configuration (``~/.config/vith/config.toml`` with
  fallback to ``~/.vithrc`` and ``~/.pyvimrc``) using ``tomllib``/``tomli`` and
  modular Python hook loading from ``~/.config/vith/hooks/`` via ``[hooks]``
  with example configs (finding 129).

Commands & editing:

- Extended ``:s`` / ``:substitute`` with ``%``, ``.``, ``$``, ``'<,'>``, and
  ``+/-N`` line ranges, bare ranged repeats (``:%s``, ``:1,3s``), arbitrary
  non-alphanumeric delimiters with ``\<delim>`` unescaping, and ``n``/``p`` flags.
- Bound ``:`` in visual selection mode to record per-buffer ``visual_marks``
  and pre-fill ``'<,'>`` in the command line.

Docs & quality gates:

- Updated ``README.md`` badges, requirements, configuration examples, and
  testing/command documentation.
- Full test suite passing: 350 passed, mypy clean on 62 source files, ruff clean.

0.13.0: 2026-11-10
-------------------

Commands, syntax highlighting & dev tooling:

Vim semantics & commands:

- Added ``:set filetype=<lang>`` and ``:set ft=<lang>`` buffer-local lexer override
  with completion support (``FiletypeCompleter``) and ``:set ft`` inspection.
- Added ``:next`` / ``:n`` and ``:previous`` / ``:prev`` / ``:N`` file cycling
  with tab-awareness (switching tabs when multiple exist) and dirty-buffer guards
  (findings 124 & 126).
- Fixed tab click handler crashing due to extra closure argument (finding 125).
- ``:compression`` (and ``:comp`` / ``:coldtext``) now opens statistics in a
  horizontal split buffer (like ``:help``) closable with ``:q``, replacing the
  terminal pager.

Tooling & quality gates:

- Added developer helper scripts (``scripts/runtest.sh``, ``scripts/type-check.sh``,
  ``scripts/lint-check-and-fix.sh``, ``scripts/code-format.sh``).
- Integrated ``pytest-cov`` and ``pytest-xdist`` for parallel test execution with
  coverage checks (85% floor enforced).
- Added comprehensive unit tests for CLI entry points (``vith.entry_points.run_vith``,
  ``vith.__main__``) and OS process title naming (``vith.process``), bringing all
  three modules to 100% test coverage.
- Full test suite passing: 311 passed, mypy clean on 59 source files, ruff clean.

0.12.1: 2026-11-09
-------------------

Bug fixes (Round 7 upstream triage, findings 116–123, all closed):

Vim semantics & key bindings:

- Added ``ZZ`` (write + quit) and ``ZQ`` (quit without saving) navigation-mode
  bindings (finding 116).
- ``Ctrl-[`` now leaves insert mode like ``Esc`` (finding 119); a numeric prefix
  before ``i``/``a`` repeats the typed text on exit, e.g. ``5itest<Esc>`` inserts
  five copies (finding 120).
- ``>>`` / ``<<`` now indent by ``tabstop``/``expandtab`` with undo support
  instead of a hardcoded width (finding 118).
- ``*`` / ``#`` record the word in search history, so ``/<Up>`` recalls it and
  bare ``:s`` reuses it (finding 122).

Commands & I/O:

- ``:w!`` force-writes read-only files (granting owner-write for one write,
  then restoring the mode); ``:wqa!`` now forwards ``force`` to each buffer
  write (finding 117).
- ``:s`` rejects nested-quantifier patterns (e.g. ``(a+)+$``) with an
  ``Unsafe pattern`` message instead of freezing on catastrophic backtracking
  (finding 123).

Highlighting:

- Extensionless files are highlighted via content sniffing (a python shebang
  pins ``PythonLexer``, otherwise ``guess_lexer`` on a 4 KiB sample), cached
  per location on both lexer branches (finding 121).

- Full test suite passing: 274 passed, mypy clean on 57 source files, ruff clean.

0.12.0: 2026-11-09
-------------------

Packaging, Thai package & modernization (since 0.11.2):

- Reorganized flat ``thai*.py`` modules into the ``vith.thai`` package
  (``classify.py``, ``clusters.py``, ``words.py``, ``patches.py``) with a lazy
  ``vith.thai_*`` compat layer and full backward compatibility.
- Adopted Python 3.10 idioms: PEP 585 built-in generics, ``str.removeprefix``,
  ``itertools.pairwise`` / ``yield from``, and ``match``/``case`` dispatch.
- Round 6 deep audit (findings 110–115, 76 items, all closed): wrong-logic fixes
  (substitute identical match, ``:wqa!``, empty-command no-op, pyflakes syntax
  errors, UTF-8 columns, cold-text undo/reset, ``HttpIO.exists``, encoding
  restore, Thai renderer guards); ``None``/bounds hardening; dead-code and
  duplication sweeps (unified splits, shared pager/lexer helpers); bounded
  caches and fast paths (lexer LRU, cell-starts guard, SARA-AM single pass);
  readability pass (nonlocal flag, explicit ``None``, PathLike/UTF-8 rc-file,
  ``EOFError``/``KeyboardInterrupt`` pager guard, byte-slice process title).
- Follow-up hardening: exotic-mapping escape fallback, desync-tolerant
  ``close_buffer``, documented compat retention.
- Full test suite passing: 250 passed, mypy clean on 57 source files, ruff clean.

0.11.2: 2026-11-09
-------------------

Bug fixes & robustness (Round 5 audit arc, 17 findings 093–109):

Vim semantics & commands:

- Fixed ``:set ic`` / ``:set ignorecase`` preview leak where aborting preview (``Esc``)
  silently kept case-insensitivity active for the remainder of the session (finding 093).
- Added support for ``:s`` flags ``i`` (ignorecase) and ``I`` (noignorecase); rejected invalid
  flags with Vim ``E488: Trailing characters`` (finding 094).
- In multi-window/multi-tab layouts, ``:q`` now checks for unsaved changes only in the
  active window's buffer instead of being blocked by dirty buffers in other windows (finding 095).
- ``:e <location>`` now checks for unsaved changes and honors ``!`` (``force``) before
  switching buffers (finding 096).
- Canonicalized untitled buffer name across status bar, ``:ls``, and buffers overlay
  to ``[New file]`` (``UNTITLED_LABEL``) (finding 107).
- Command line mutual-exclusion flags (``-p``, ``-o``, ``-O``) raise ``ValueError`` defensively
  inside ``load_initial_files`` instead of a bare assert (finding 107).

Thai & Lao script support & renderer:

- Reorganized flat ``thai*.py`` files (``thai.py``, ``thai_classify.py``, ``thai_clusters.py``,
  ``thai_words.py``) into a dedicated ``vith.thai`` package (``classify.py``, ``clusters.py``,
  ``words.py``, ``patches.py``) with full backward compatibility.
- Sticky Thai renderer gate is now latched on multi-line paste, undo/redo, and full-text
  assignments when Thai text is introduced on non-cursor rows (finding 097).
- Re-entrant differential renderer calls now reliably restore ``screen.zero_width_escapes``
  under an outer ``try/finally`` block (finding 098).
- Hoisted Thai cluster calculation imports in ``ColdTextBuffer._cursor_vertical`` to module
  level, eliminating per-keystroke import overhead on ``j``/``k`` (finding 102).
- Added ``_cell_has_sara_am`` fast-path check in ``_sanitize_and_invalidate_sara_am`` to skip
  key sorting and set allocations on rows without SARA AM (finding 109).

Performance, storage & completion:

- Rewrote ``BufferListOverlay.highlight_location`` to produce chunked token spans rather than
  per-character fragments and loops (finding 109).
- Expanded ``DocumentWordsCompleter`` cache key with ``line_start`` to detect text shifts on lines
  prior to the cursor line (finding 109).
- Preserved original trailing newline status across buffer save and reload (``EditorBuffer.write``),
  ensuring files without an ending newline do not acquire one unconditionally (finding 103).
- Fixed ``_LazyStylesDict`` containment: ``__getitem__`` raises ``KeyError`` on unknown styles so that
  standard ``Mapping.__contains__`` (``'style' in editor.styles``) returns ``False`` instead of raising
  ``ClassNotFound`` (finding 103).
- Fixed example ``vithrc`` F9 execution callback to guard against ``None`` buffer and abort on write
  failures (finding 103).

Testing, tooling & packaging:

- ``tools/bench_quez_cold_text.py`` benchmarks shipped ``vith.cold_text.ColdTextStack`` instead of a
  private duplicate, with corrected ``measure_ms`` naming and fixture truncation (finding 099).
- Refreshed reproducible benchmark figures in ``docs/speed_latency_plan.md`` (finding 100).
- Repaired vacuous/flaky assertions in tests, replaced inspect-based tests with functional execution,
  and cleaned up unused mock assignments (finding 101).
- Updated packaging and documentation floors: prompt_toolkit ``>=3.0.0,<3.1.0``, cleaned dead
  ``setup.py`` and ``requirements-dev.txt`` references, added tool cache directories to ``.gitignore``
  (finding 104).
- Cleaned up build/dist release artifacts from source tree (finding 105).
- Dead code cleanup across decorators, previewers, classifier sets, and cold-text metadata (finding 106).
- Type-annotated ``current_editor_buffer -> EditorBuffer | None`` with explicit ``return None`` and
  corrected ``is_thai_base`` docstring (finding 108).
- Full test suite passing: 217 passed, 1 skipped, mypy clean on 56 source files, ruff clean.

0.11.1: 2026-11-09
-------------------

Bug fixes:

Thai & Lao script support:

- Visual-block selection (``<C-v>``) on lines containing SARA AM (``U+0E33``) or
  fewer combining marks than corner rows no longer overshoots mid-line:
  ``_thai_selection_range_at_line`` and ``_thai_selection_ranges`` clamp
  selection bounds strictly to cell-cluster boundaries within line margins
  instead of unconditionally bleeding ``prompt_toolkit`` codepoint columns
  (finding 092).

Documentation & audit:

- OKF v0.2 documentation bundle synchronized to 92 machine-verified findings:
  cataloged finding 092, resolved missing Round 3 Addendum table in
  ``docs/bugs/index.md``, and synchronized update logs.

0.11.0: 2026-11-08
-------------------

Field-verified correctness arcs since 0.10.0 (documented in detail in
``docs/bugs/index.md``: 91 machine-verified findings, all closed; every fix
carries regression tests):

Thai & Lao script support:

- Visual-mode correctness: visual selections, visual blocks and block
  ``I``/``A`` insert positions align on **cell-cluster columns** — Thai/Lao
  clusters highlight, cut, yank and insert like Vim cells (findings 076-085).
- ``j``/``k`` keep the *visual* column across Thai rows (``preferred_column``
  was a raw codepoint column; finding 078).
- Word spans no longer slice mixed-script clusters (Latin base + Thai mark,
  generic accents) for ``iw``/``aw``/``*``/``#`` (finding 086).
- Cluster-safe counted operations: counted ``$`` (``3$``), line-local
  ``e``/``E`` snapping, whole-cell ``2rX``, counted ``~`` respecting
  ``:set tildeop`` (findings 053, 063, 071).
- ``:s`` with a Thai replacement re-arms the SARA-AM neighbor sanitizer; gate
  latching/decay covers Thai file names and message banners
  (findings 081, 082).

Editor commands & buffers:

- ``:b`` fixes: untitled-buffer crash (080), completed patterns jumping, a
  1-based numbering shared by ``:b <n>``/``:ls``/``BufferListOverlay`` and
  ``[New file]`` names (findings 067, 080, 087).
- ``:s`` flags parsing (``:s/x/y//g``, ``gg``, multi-letter flags) with
  ``:0,1s/`` mapping to the first line (finding 083).
- ``:e`` on a file deleted since it was read shows E211-style error and keeps
  the in-memory contents (finding 088).
- ``:q``/``:wqa`` window-vs-exit semantics; ``:bd`` across tabs keeps the
  invariant (findings 066, 067, 070).
- ``__main__`` import guard, reporter invalidation, aborted ``:set`` preview
  leak fix (``:set paste`` × ``Esc``), I/O robustness (latin-1 → utf-8 save
  fallback, unknown-backend read-only buffers), first-run startup fixes
  (findings 068, 069, 091, 070).

Performance & maintenance:

- Thai ``j``/``k`` cell-start scans cached with LRU (~762 µs per keypress on
  2000-codepoint rows → O(1)); megabyte line span-cache bypass; lazy-import
  hoists in the cursor path; ``:s`` single-split reuse (finding 090).
- ``thai.py`` split into ``thai_classify``/``thai_clusters``/``thai_words``;
  the prompt_toolkit patch installer moved out of import time into
  ``Editor.__init__`` (finding 075).
- Dead-code sweep including a working ``.vithrc`` example; duplicate ``:set``
  logic consolidated into a single catalog; duplicate word-walk logic unified
  into one generator (findings 073, 074).

0.10.0: 2026-11-08
------------------

Cold text:

- Compressed undo/redo history via ``quez``: snapshots are stored compressed
  with Zstandard level 1 by default. Configure with
  ``editor.cold_text_compression`` in ``.vithrc`` (``zstd``, ``zlib``,
  ``zlib-fast``, ``zlib-best``, ``lzo`` or ``none``). Inspect current buffer
  statistics with ``:compression``.
- Added the ``lzo`` optional dependency extra.

0.9.1: 2026-11-08
-----------------

Packaging:

- Fix PyPI author credits metadata rendering in pyproject.toml (PEP 621).

0.9.0: 2026-11-08
-----------------

Forking and rebranding to Vith (Vi + Thai support)

- Renamed project from pyvim to vith: PEP 621 packaging
  (setup.py → pyproject.toml), Python 3.10+ requirement, console script `vith`,
  README.md with fork attribution; BSD 3-clause license retained with stacked
  copyright (© 2015-2023 Jonathan Slenders, © 2026 Chaiwat Suttipongsakul);
  upstream repository linked to https://github.com/prompt-toolkit/pyvim;
  original PyVim changelog preserved verbatim below as historical appendix.

Stability, performance and international input:

- Fixed the Python 3.14+/3.15 ``asyncio.get_event_loop()`` startup crash:
  opening any file before the event loop runs no longer aborts ``vith``.
- Added Thai & Lao script support: terminal cell-cluster navigation and
  edits (``h``, ``l``, ``j``, ``k``, ``x``, ``X``, ``s``, ``r``, ``~``, ``$``,
  ``e``...), two-tier Thai word segmentation (libthai, with an
  orthographic fallback), and SARA AM (U+0E33/U+0EB3) differential renderer
  fixes. See ``docs/thai_support_plan.md``.
- Latency work (``docs/speed_latency_plan.md``): streaming + cached
  Pygments highlighting, per-line word-span caching for Thai word
  motions, lazy colorscheme loading, singleton word completion cache and
  an O(1) pyflakes error index.

Bug fixes (machine-verified findings bundle, ``docs/bugs/``):

- ``:s`` with a line range beyond EOF reports ``E19`` instead of crashing;
  the cursor lands on the last substituted line.
- jedi is optional: ``.py`` completion falls back to word completion when
  jedi is not installed instead of crashing.
- A failed ``:w`` no longer terminates the editor through ``:wq``/``:wqa``;
  unknown locations report an error without side effects.
- ReportingProcessor runs before tab expansion so pyflakes error columns
  stay aligned on tab-indented lines, and the message toolbar shows all
  errors of the cursor line.
- Buffer numbering inserts new buffers after the active one; command
  grammar alternation is deterministic.

Tooling and packaging:

- Added ruff (lint + format) and a mypy baseline checked against the
  packaging floor; ``tox`` setup replaced by ``pyproject.toml [project.optional-dependencies] dev``.
- Python floor is now ``python_requires='>=3.10'``; prompt_toolkit floor
  raised to 3.0; ``six`` and the python 2 directives removed.


